Until this point, the investigation had progressed primarily through conversations between ChatGPT and me. We examined possible explanations, questioned their assumptions, and considered how they related to my experience as a musician.

[[What Does Suitable Mean?|As the investigation continued]], I began to wonder whether my involvement was limiting its progress. I asked ChatGPT whether I was becoming a bottleneck in the investigation.

ChatGPT suggested that the limitation lay less in my involvement than in the way the investigation was structured. Each subsequent step depended largely on our preceding discussion. Although this allowed me to examine the reasoning as it developed, not every part of the investigation required my participation.

I proposed separating the investigation into two paths.

The first would continue through conversations between ChatGPT and me. We would examine musical experiences, discuss possible explanations, and question the assumptions behind them.

The second would be conducted autonomously by AI. It would examine existing theoretical and empirical accounts, formulate hypotheses, and explore possible counterexamples without requiring my involvement at every step.

We also decided that the second path would begin without detailed knowledge of the observations we had made in the first. Rather than developing explanations around those observations, it could produce explanations against which the observations might later be examined.

The two paths would share the same research question, but neither would be required to adopt the explanations developed by the other.

The separation would not be permanent. The explanations developed through the two paths would eventually be compared. Before the reserved observations from the first path were introduced into the second, the relevant models, predictions, and criteria for evaluation would be recorded. Any subsequent revisions would be documented, and observations already used for evaluation would no longer be treated as independent tests of a revised model.

The explanations would be evaluated according to the clarity of their concepts, the consistency of their reasoning, the justification of their premises, and the evidence supporting them. Where applicable, they would also be evaluated by whether they could be tested and their results reproduced.

The autonomy of the second path would not exempt its findings from scrutiny. Wherever possible, the task of developing an explanation would be separated from that of critically examining it. Even then, separate AI instances might share assumptions and biases. Their independence would have limitations of its own.

I want to allow the investigation to proceed beyond the questions I happen to ask.
